window.products.push({"id":267109,"name":"Small Space Heater Oscillating Heater, LC-POWER Electric Ceramic Heater with Thermostat,Overheat and Tip-Over Protection,PTC Fast Heating for Office b","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61rusVLD6TL._AC_SL1140_.jpg","description":"ABOUT LC-POWER Electric Space Heater: Pattern: White Small HeaterHeating Method: Ceramic, Fan & forced air,Fast Heating.ETL Certificated. OPERATION The appliance requires no installation; it should be used solely as a portable appliance.  - Turn the thermostat knob in a clockwise direction until it reaches the maximum setting. - Summer service (ventilation only): turn the knob to setting. - Heating at reduced power: turn the switch knob to setting I (600W). - Heating at full power: turn the switch knob to setting II (1200W).  - Switching off: turn the switch knob to setting O. Attention: 1. During the first few minutes of initial use, you may notice a slight odour and some smoke,don't worry,this is normal and will dissipate quickly. It is the coating applied to the heating elements to prevent rusting during transit. 2.Before Plugging the unit into the mains, ensure by visual inspection that the unit is intact and has not suffered any damage during transit. 3. In order to avoid overheating,do not cover it while in operation. This will prevent circulate. 4. CAUTION Please make sure to put the heater on a FLAT, HARD,STABLE surface. Otherwise, the \"tip-over sensor\" will be triggered. REGULATING THE THERMOSTAT When the room has reached the required temperature,turn the right thermostat knob (where included) in an anti-clockwise direction up to the point where the appliance switches off and not beyond.The temperature fixed in this way will be automatically regulated and kept at a constant level by the thermostat. OVER HEATING PROTECTION There is a safety device inside which will switch off the heater in case of accidental overheating (eg. Obstruction of air intake and outlet grilles, motor turning slowly or not at all). To reset, disconnect the plug from the power for a few minutes,remove the cause of overheating then plug the appliance in.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61rusVLD6TL._AC_SL1140_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"LC-Power","source_asin":"B09H345V5M","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-267109","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09H345V5M","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B09H345V5M","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
